This product includes logic derived from third-party software.

The zenoh gate (crates/oxhubd/src/chat/zgate/) links the Eclipse zenoh
1.10.1 crates zenoh-protocol, zenoh-codec and zenoh-buffers for the wire
types and encoding, and implements the accepting side of the zenoh unicast
establishment and transport (InitSyn/InitAck/OpenSyn/OpenAck, frames,
fragments, keep-alive, sequence-number masks) in its own code after
io/zenoh-transport of the same release. No zenoh source file is copied.

The subscriber-side bandwidth estimation and simulcast layer allocation
(crates/oxsfud/src/sim/bwe.rs, crates/oxsfud/src/sim/alloc.rs,
crates/oxsfud/src/sim/core.rs) are re-implemented in Rust from the
mediasoup 3.32.2 BWE stack (worker/src/RTC/BWE, ISC License), whose core
congestion control and bandwidth estimation logic is in turn derived from
libwebrtc (BSD 3-Clause License). Parts are taken from libwebrtc directly
(modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc, modules/pacing). A file and line
mapping is kept in the specification repository
(spec/server/sim_loop/DESIGN.md).

